nivaqi — authors and copyright holders
======================================

nivaqi (நிவதி) is authored by two people. This file says who, so that "who
wrote this" has a single answer rather than several.

  Isha Maruff <isha@etamil.in>
      Author and copyright holder, 2026-present.

      Two addresses, and each is used where it does its job:

        **isha@etamil.in** is the contact and copyright address. It is the
        one in this file, in the source headers and in the documentation.

        **icykki26@gmail.com** is the address on the GitHub account the
        nivaqi repositories live under, so it is the address on the commits.
        GitHub links a commit to an account by matching the author's email,
        and the account's own address needs nothing verified to match.

      One person. If the contact address is ever added and verified on that
      account, the commits can move to it and this paragraph can go.

  Esan Maruff <esan@etamil.in>
      Author and copyright holder, 2026-present.

      One person, two names, each used where it does its job:

        **Esan Maruff** is the name on GitHub (@Maruff), on every other
        account, on etamil.in and throughout the commit history. It is what a
        reader sees and what he prefers to be addressed as.

        **Mohammed Maruff** is the legal name and the name on the published
        research. In eTamil, copyright is asserted in it. nivaqi's source
        headers name both authors in the short form; if a legal name is ever
        needed in the headers, change it there and here together.


COPYRIGHT NOTICE

Every nivaqi source file carries:

    // SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
    // Copyright (C) 2026 Isha Maruff and Esan Maruff


LICENCE

AGPL-3.0-or-later. See LICENSE.

nivaqi imports nUlakam, the eTamil standard library, which is AGPL-3.0-or-later
in Maruff/eTamil_lang. All nivaqi repositories are public, so the licences are
consistent and nothing turns on the boundary between them.

See docs/DECISIONS/0008-repositories-and-licence.md for the one licensing
question that is still open — it concerns the separate private products (AI, BI
and the Customizing Studio), not this repository.


CONTRIBUTIONS

None yet. Contributors will be added here as they arrive.

Copyright is not assigned to the project. A contributor keeps copyright in what
they wrote and licenses it under AGPL-3.0-or-later. That means this file stops
being a list of two people and becomes the list of everyone the licence has to
be honoured towards.

Before accepting a first external contribution, read
docs/DECISIONS/0008-repositories-and-licence.md: whether a contributor licence
agreement is wanted is a decision with a closing window, not an open one.


GIT COMMIT AUTHORSHIP

Separate from this file, and the owner's to configure. Nothing in this
repository changes it.
